  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 205 PM MDT MON SEP 14 2026\nThe end of the work week will remain unsettled, with an upper-\nlevel low pressure system moving overhead. Precipitation chances\nwill be highest in the west-central Idaho mountains (50-70%\nchance), with mentionable chances elsewhere (15-40% chance),\nlowest in the valleys. After this system moves out, an upper-\nlevel ridge will build into the NW U.S., bringing a clearing and\nwarming trend back to the area. Models are split on the forecast\nstarting next week, but a return to another unsettled pattern\nlooks to return.",
